※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4606

※ A record is what has fields to answer.  A sum holds one of its parts rather than all
※ of them, so what its fields are has no one answer; a tuple's members have no names;
※ and everything else is one value.
※
※ A generic definition asks `⎕isrecord` first, in a condition the compiler settles, and
※ reaches this only where it did not.

type Either = left: u8 | right: u16

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let e: Either = Either(.left ← 1u8)
    comptime foreach f := ⎕fields(e):
        ⎕drop(f⟦0⟧)
    0u6
